  data: {
    LLM: "If you have a high piece (12, 11, 10), keeping is usually safe. If you have a low piece (0, Pot, Fool), you MUST swap. The danger lies in the middle pieces (5, 6, 7)â€”swapping might get you a Matador (death) or a lower piece.\n\nReading Neighbors: If the player to your right swaps with you and gives you a Fool, you are now desperate. You must swap to your left. If your left neighbor looks confident (Matador?), you are trapped.\n\nThe 'Blieken' Bluff: Pretending to hesitate with a high piece to catch a neighbor swapping.",
